  "question": {
    "text": "As per de-Broglie's formula a macroscopic particle of mass $100 \\mathrm{g}$ and moving at a velocity of $100 \\mathrm{cm} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ will have a wavelength of",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nY09o",
      "text": "$6.6 \\times 10^{-29} \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6BTAg",
      "text": "$6.6 \\times 10^{-30} \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Yl5CD",
      "text": "$6.6 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nfJMq",
      "text": "$6.6 \\times 10^{-32} \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to de-Broglie. wavelength, $\\lambda=\\frac{h}{m v}$\r\nGiven, $\\quad m=100 \\mathrm{g}, v=100 \\mathrm{cm} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}$\r\nand\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nh &=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{J}-\\mathrm{s} \\\\\r\n&=6.6 \\times 10^{-27} \\mathrm{erg}-\\mathrm{s}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\nOn substituting values, we get\r\n$$\r\n\\lambda=\\frac{6.6 \\times 10^{-27}}{100 \\times 100}=6.6 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{cm}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
